the VW Beetle in all colors and  variations  German Mexican and Brazilian beetles old  and new beetles they've all come  together for the beetles sunshine tour  the world's largest beetle gathering  they rendezvous at Lubeck Airport and  form a seemingly never-ending convoy on  the roads of northern Germany it's the  tenth anniversary for this annual bug  collection a milestone that the tour's  initiator Gabriella crafts is  justifiably proud of she points out that  the beetle sunshine tour has itself  attained cult status for the  participants it's like a family reunion  they come from Italy Sweden the Czech  Republic Slovakia Poland Austria and  every year the Netherlands - beetle  drivers will find each other no matter  where they are the four hundred and  seventy colorful bugs migrate to the bug  man garden a large field right on  Covenanters baltic coast  some veterans have been on board from  the very beginning like hands yoga and  shorts he says the first time just 68  bugs assembled near the car dealership  and drove on a little tour and it grew  from there  more beetle owners showed up every year  and the gathering moved to the main  fairground in krumitz eventually that  got to be too small and it moved to tava  mandir but this year the grounds here  are barely large enough to hold all the  cars over time many of the beetle  drivers have made lots of friends at the  gatherings they get together once or  twice a year generally at the sunshine  tour that's what keeps many of them  coming back the drivers span three  generations the obsession with the cult  car has just kept going and going and  going for over 75 years but not everyone  here owns a beetle many are just here  for the spectacle zippy glitter owner of  the beetle fire engine has his own  theories about what the attraction  really is  the illusion he explains that he fights  other things besides fires he fights  boredom many of the people in attendance  here would like to own cars like these  so he's here to help put out the fires  of longing longing for a Beatle being  crazy is encouraged here the beetle  owners express themselves through their  cars this is one place where dogs aren't  allowed to scratch they have bugs beetle  owner dieter Gerda says that they had  the dogs first then bought the car and  airbrushed it to match custom jobs range  from kitsch to art this Western  rust-bucket  embodies one or maybe the other  the line between the two is fuzzy even  when it comes to accessories and tuning  Beauty is quite often in the eye of the  beholder even Santa Claus sent three of  his helpers to the gathering beetle fan  Christiana poor man had the idea the  year before but didn't go through with  it until this year when she thought she  could be a little more creative and this  was the result the get together would  hardly be complete without home bake  cookies the neon chartreuse of this  custom paint job was not available from  the factory even if many other colors  were Beatle tuner Sascha bloom explains  this had always been his dream car and  when he saw this color he liked it right  off originally the bug was blue one  winter he took it apart and painted  everything for everyday use he's got a  black beetle this one's just for show  there's no end to beetle owners  creativity  okay the variety makes for the spice of  life and the party mood all around  another sunshine tour veteran is tuner  Sydney Hoffman he shows how to get a big  sound and power out of a little car  he-man he explains that this is the  highest increment of performance  enhancement at 370 horsepower this is  the new air intake made of real carbon  fiber the diameter was enlarged to  produce more power you need fresh air to  supply the bigger turbo injection this  provides it Travie mandir is a popular  seaside resort in summer and all the  more so when the VW Beetle fans start  partying all along the boardwalks  happybirthday sunshine tour will be back  next year
 

